  (lib_symbols)

  (text "═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
                       CLOCK DISTRIBUTION (RECEIVE ONLY)
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

ARCHITECTURE CHANGE (Rev 2.0):
──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Rev 1.0: Local 20 MHz TCXO (DSC1001DI2-020) + NC7SZ125 buffer
  Rev 2.0: SCLK provided by carrier FPGA over B2B connector

  DELETED:
    • Y1 (DSC1001DI2-020 TCXO) — removed
    • U_CLK (NC7SZ125 buffer) — removed
    • R_TERM (22Ω series termination) — removed
    • C_CLK1, C_CLK2 (oscillator decoupling) — removed
    • TP_CLK (clock test point at buffer output) — removed

RATIONALE:
  The carrier FPGA generates SCLK for deterministic timing of both
  RHD2164 chips. A single clock source eliminates skew between
  headstage and carrier, and removes a digital switching noise source
  from the analog headstage.

──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

CLOCK PATH (Rev 2.0):
──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  Carrier FPGA ──► B2B Connector (J5) ──► SCLK net on headstage
                                     │
                                     ├──► RHD2164 U1 SCLK pin
                                     │
                                     └──► RHD2164 U2 SCLK pin

  Carrier-side responsibilities:
    • Generate 20 MHz SCLK (or variable, per sample rate setting)
    • Series termination at FPGA output (22–47Ω, carrier-side)
    • Clock jitter spec: <5 ps RMS (adequate for 30 kS/s)

  Headstage-side:
    • Clean routing from B2B connector to both AFE chips
    • Route on Layer 4 (digital signals) over solid Layer 5 DGND
    • Keep ≥3 mm separation from electrode/analog traces on Layer 1
    • No layer transitions in SCLK path on headstage
    • TP_SCLK test point at fan-out node (1 mm pad)

  OPTIONAL: If signal integrity requires it, place a single-gate
  buffer (NC7SZ125 or 74LVC1G125) on headstage to re-drive SCLK.
  Footprint reserved but DNI by default.

──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

CLOCK BOM (Rev 2.0 — headstage only):
──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Ref       Value       Package      Part Number       Notes
──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
R_SCLK    33Ω         0402         -                 Optional damping at
                                                     RHD2164 input (DNI)
TP_SCLK   Test point  1mm pad      -                 Clock verification
──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

LAYOUT NOTES:
  • SCLK trace: controlled impedance 50Ω microstrip on L4
  • Length-match SCLK to U1 and U2 within ±2 mm
  • Guard with GND vias along SCLK route if crossing near analog
  • No stubs — star topology from B2B pin to U1/U2

═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════"
